e\" whose exponentiated and normalized forms yield attention, diffusion-maps, and magnetic diffusion. And use product of experts and Schrödinger-bridges to connect and organize them into equilibrium, nonequilibrium steady-state, and driven dynamics.\nL17: Subjects:  | Machine Learning (cs.LG)\nL18: Cite as:  | cite9†arXiv:2604.09560 [cs.LG]\nL19:    | (or cite10†arXiv:2604.09560v1 [cs.LG] for this version)\nL20:    | cite11†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2604.09560†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL21: ## Submission history\nL22: \nL23: From: Julio Candanedo [cite12†view email ]\nL24: [v1] Wed, 11 Feb 2026 17:27:34 UTC (43 KB)\nL25: cite5†[v2] Wed, 19 Aug 2026 15:34:15 UTC (8,447 KB)\nL26: \nL27: Full-text links:\nL28: \nL29: ## Access Paper:\nL30: \nL31: View a PDF of the paper titled The Diffusion-Attention Connection, by Julio Candanedo\nL32: \nL33:   * cite7†View PDF L34:   * cite8†HTML (experimental) L35:   * cite13†TeX Source L36: \nL37: cite14†view license L38: \nL39: ### Current browse context:\nL40: \nL41: cs.LG\nL42: \nL43: cite15†< prev |   cite16†next > L44: \nL45: cite17†new | cite18†recent | cite19†2026-04 L46: \nL47: Change to browse by:\nL48: \nL49: cite20†cs L50: ### References & Citations\nL51: \nL52:   * cite21†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L53:   * cite22†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L54:   * cite23†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L55: \nL56: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL57: \nL58: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL59: \nL60: [Button: ×]\nL61: \nL62: loading...\nL63: \nL64: Data provided by:\nL65: \nL66: ### Bookmark\nL67: \nL68: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL69: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL70: \nL71: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL72: \nL73: Bibliographic Explorer (cite24†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org )\nL74: \nL75: [Input] Connected Papers Toggle\nL76: \nL77: Connected Papers (cite25†What is Connected Papers?†www.connectedpaper